      "No vendor checkpoint weights, safetensors tensor headers or real vendor tokenizer are loaded for this family; all displayed numerical weights, token IDs, activations and gradients are [micro].",
      "Micro capacity is 4 layers, hidden width 32, intermediate width 48, 8 query heads, 1 KV head, head dimension 8, a 4-token local window and 4 experts selecting 2 per token. This preserves the 8:1 grouped-query ratio, but changes the expert selection fraction from 4/32 to 2/4.",
      "The teaching model uses short-context full-dimension RoPE; the checkpoint uses YaRN context extension.",
      "MXFP4 expert quantization and large-scale load-balancing training are not reproduced.",
      "The micro reference evaluates every candidate expert, then combines only selected top-k outputs with zero weights for the others. It demonstrates sparse-routing numerics, not the compute savings of a production sparse expert kernel."
    ],
    "mechanisms": {
      "norm": "x / sqrt(mean(x²)+eps) × weight",
      "attention": "softmax(concat(QKᵀ/√head_dim + causal/local mask, learned_sink))[:token_count] × V",
      "routing": "selected=top_k(router(x)); weights=softmax(selected logits); output=sum(weights_e × expert_e(x))",
      "ffn": "g=min(gate,7); u=clip(up,−7,7); down(g × sigmoid(1.702g) × (u+1))",
